cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use or refer to this software, please cite it using these metadata.
type: software
title: "dpa-and-data-transfer-review: deterministic, cited GDPR Art. 28 and Chapter V transfer checks"
abstract: >-
  A standard-library Python command-line tool that checks a structured description of a Data
  Processing Agreement for the elements GDPR Art. 28(2)-(4) and Art. 33(2) require, and assesses
  the Chapter V basis of every international transfer, per destination and per sub-processor. It
  writes a cited review packet with a visible review state and a gating exit code. It is not legal
  advice, and all bundled data is synthetic.
authors:
  - family-names: Förste
    given-names: Sebastian
repository-code: "https://github.com/sebastianfoerste/dpa-and-data-transfer-review"
url: "https://github.com/sebastianfoerste/dpa-and-data-transfer-review"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
keywords:
  - gdpr
  - dsgvo
  - data processing agreement
  - avv
  - international data transfers
  - standard contractual clauses
  - legal engineering
  - compliance as code
